From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:16:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/30] drama: the speech codec, with codec.pth read without
 Python

The codec decodes ten codebooks a frame to mono 44.1 kHz PCM, 2048 samples a frame, as the reference's FP16
vocoder does: RVQ, the windowed post-module transformer, two upsample stages and the DAC decoder. codec_pth.zig
reads torch.save's zip archive and runs its state-dict pickle on a VM that knows only the opcodes and globals a
tensor state dict uses, so nothing in the file runs. Weight norm is folded in FP32 and tensors are cast to FP16
with round-to-nearest-even, as the reference does.
